# Always-on Plain-English completion voice

Every user-facing completion (final Cursor message, PR body, written report, checkpoint, handover) **must open with friendly conversational English**.

This is required **even when the prompt does not mention Plain-English, a report, or a summary**. Silence in the prompt is not a waiver.

Do **not** open with git SHAs, “Starting main SHA”, checkout logs, numbered engineering checklists, file lists, or commit-style bullets. Technical detail may follow after the Plain-English lead.

See `AGENTS.md` and `docs/v1-reference-pack/LUME_DEVELOPMENT_AND_EVALUATION_ROADMAP_V1.md` §19.
